[center][size=6][b][color=#b48cff]VISUAL SOUL GEMS[/color][/b][/size]
[size=4][i]Filled soul gems should look filled.[/i][/size][/center]

Visual Soul Gems — VSG — gives filled vanilla and black soul gems distinct visual effects in OpenMW.

For vanilla soul gems, VSG uses the excellent [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/48300][color=#b48cff]Crystal Soul Gems[/color][/url] assets by SVNR, OffworldDevil, and NullCascade.

Pick one of four styles, or let VSG roll the dice.

[size=4][b][color=#b48cff]WHAT IT DOES[/color][/b][/size]

Crystal Soul Gems normally ships its effect variants as alternatives: one set of meshes overwrites another, so you pick a look at install time.

[color=#b48cff][b]VSG wants all of them available at once.[/b][/color]

VSG bundles the required meshes so all four styles can coexist without overwriting one another.

You do [b]not[/b] need to install Crystal Soul Gems separately. VSG already includes the assets it needs.

VSG only changes [b]filled[/b] soul gems. Empty gems are left alone.

[size=4][b][color=#b48cff]VISUAL VARIANTS[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Particles[/b][/*]
[*][b]Particles & Static Glow[/b][/*]
[*][b]Static Glow[/b][/*]
[*][b][color=#b48cff]Ultra Glow[/color][/b] — default[/*]
[/list]

You can also enable [b]Randomize[/b], which chooses a random variant whenever VSG converts a filled soul gem or stack.

The settings menu is available in English, German, Spanish, French, and Swedish.

[size=4][b][color=#b48cff]HOW IT WORKS[/color][/b][/size]

When VSG finds a filled soul gem in the world, it replaces it with a matching visual variant.

OpenMW still treats the replacement as a soul gem. VSG preserves the trapped soul, stack count, ownership, scale, and placement while changing only its appearance.

[color=#b48cff][b]Stacks stay stacks. Souls stay trapped.[/b][/color] The pretty lights are the only part meant to change.

VSG handles all five vanilla soul gem sizes: Petty, Lesser, Common, Greater, and Grand.

VSG also recognizes filled black soul gems from [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/45902][color=#b48cff]Black Soul Gems[/color][/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/49042][color=#b48cff]OAAB Data[/color][/url], and gives them the same four visual styles.

[b]One important detail:[/b] once VSG has converted a soul gem, that object keeps the variant it received. Changing the setting later affects future conversions; it does not retroactively repaint already-converted gems.

[size=4][b][color=#b48cff]REQUIREMENTS[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]OpenMW 0.51.0 or newer[/b][/*]
[/list]

That's it.

Crystal Soul Gems is [b]not[/b] a separate requirement. The necessary assets are bundled because VSG needs the different mesh variants to exist side-by-side instead of overwriting one another.

[size=4][b][color=#b48cff]INSTALLATION[/color][/b][/size]

Install VSG as a normal OpenMW data directory and enable the mod.

Keep the bundled meshes and textures with it. Do not cherry-pick the individual Crystal Soul Gems option folders over VSG; VSG has already reorganized the files into the layout it needs.

[size=4][b][color=#b48cff]COMPATIBILITY[/color][/b][/size]

VSG uses its own visual records for converted filled soul gems. Conventional mesh replacers that change the original soul gem paths therefore will not affect gems already converted by VSG.

Empty soul gems are not converted by VSG.

[size=4][b][color=#b48cff]UNINSTALLATION[/color][/b][/size]

VSG is not a simple mesh replacer. Once a soul gem has been converted, your save may contain a VSG-specific version of that item.

[color=#b48cff][b]Mid-save uninstallation is unsupported.[/b][/color] Removing VSG can leave already-converted soul gems pointing to assets that no longer exist.

[size=4][b][color=#b48cff]CREDITS[/color][/b][/size]

VSG bundles assets from [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/48300][b][color=#b48cff]Crystal Soul Gems[/color][/b][/url], created by [b]SVNR, OffworldDevil, and NullCascade[/b] and uploaded by [b]SVNR[/b].

Those files are redistributed under the permissions published on the original Nexus Mods page. Crystal Soul Gems does not permit its assets to be used in mods/files that are sold and does not permit mods using those assets to earn Nexus Donation Points, so [b]VSG does not participate in Donation Points[/b].

The filled black soul gem NIFs were made by [b][color=#b48cff]grumblingvomit[/color][/b], based on [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/49042][color=#b48cff]OAAB Data[/color][/url] assets.

Please go endorse the original. These meshes are the whole reason VSG gets to look this good.

Disclaimer: LLMs were used in the production of this mod's documentation, but not the mod itself, as LLMs sucked when this mod was actually made.
